                <pb facs="0412" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg304"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/674: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-06-18T13:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 18, 1927—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 18—7:12
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>656. Your 257, June 16, 6 p.m. I have instructed Jacobs June 17, 4 p.m., in
                    accordance with paragraph No. 2 of the Legation’s 646, June 16, 4 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
